WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.203 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.236
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:04.236 --> 00:00:05.371
I'm just gonna
come around and say

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:06.772
I don't know how
today's gonna go.

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:10.309
I'm feeling
a little out of sorts.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:15.180
It's lauded, not "louded."

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.651
Nevada, not "Nevahda."

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:22.755
We showed a picture
of Grimace's skeleton.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:26.559
Someone wrote, "Grimace
wouldn't have a skeleton,

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:29.996
because he's an eggplant."

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:35.802
And I thought,
"That can't be possible."

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:38.070
I mean, though he is
kind of a dick,

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.642
but it's grosser
'cause I dug into it,

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:46.212
and according to a McDonald's
manager a few years ago,

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:49.349
Grimace is based
on a taste bud.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.655
And if that's true,
Grimace is just a terrible name.

00:00:56.655 --> 00:01:01.026
Anyway, next time
you look at Grimace,

00:01:01.026 --> 00:01:03.263
he's that.

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.631
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:06.932
I know you might not see
Grimace there,

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:10.170
but we did get a little bit
closer on a taste bud,

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.571
and you see him
a little bit better there.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:16.309
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.344
I showed a picture yesterday,

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:21.514
I guess, of a baby with a goatee

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:26.719
and said, "This has been
'Seth puts a goatee on a baby

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:28.988
because the news is so bad',"
some version of that.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:30.189
Way too many of you jumped out

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.458
and said you didn't put
a goatee on a baby,

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:33.560
graphics did.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.161
Don't.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.696
Don't make them your friends.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.330
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.266
I see what you're doing,
but don't.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.838
Don't be the teen girl
in a '50s movie

00:01:45.838 --> 00:01:49.375
who starts dating the bad boy
to make your parents mad.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.010
Just don't do it.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:56.649
Baze and I talked about this
after last week's correction.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.351
We talked about, and a lot
of you were surprised --

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:04.423
Timmy never fell down the well
in the TV show "Lassie."

00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:06.759
Which is weird because I think
it's what a lot of us

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:10.629
would think was most certainly
a thing that happened

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:11.931
on the show "Lassie."

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:15.034
And this is known
as the Mandela effect,

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.470
which is when we believe
a thing to be true

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.371
that didn't actually happen.

00:02:19.371 --> 00:02:24.009
It was coined in 2009 by a woman
who believed that,

00:02:24.009 --> 00:02:26.446
in the '80s,
Nelson Mandela had died in jail.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:28.414
And then she realized
that a lot of other people

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:31.484
shared that memory of a thing
that didn't happen.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:34.353
And so a lot of people
have made a list

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:37.624
of certain things
that we get wrong,

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:40.260
such as Timmy falling in a well,

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:45.297
that are examples
of the Mandela effect.

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:46.932
Some famous film and TV quotes.

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:52.705
for example, the line is not,
"Luke, I am your father."

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.873
The line is,
"No, I am your father."

00:02:54.873 --> 00:02:56.175
That surprised me --
wouldn't you think,

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.110
based on every piece
of comedy you've seen,

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.078
it's "Luke, I am your father"?

00:03:00.078 --> 00:03:01.547
"Beam me up, Scotty,"

00:03:01.547 --> 00:03:05.618
never uttered
on the show "Star Trek."

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:08.787
The closest was,
"Scotty, beam me up."

00:03:08.787 --> 00:03:12.358
Obviously, the same point,

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:14.393
but I would have put money
on the fact that it was

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:15.495
"Beam me up, Scotty."

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:19.097
And this shocked me
the most of all,

00:03:19.097 --> 00:03:20.433
I guess, on this show,

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:24.370
I've never actually said,
"It's time for 'A Closer Look.'"

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.239
I say, "Now do 'A Closer Look.'

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:28.641
I don't see why not."

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:36.182
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:41.487
Pence -- we had a version
of Pence getting beamed up.

00:03:43.655 --> 00:03:47.726
Built in transitions here
in today's corrections.

00:03:47.726 --> 00:03:50.763
But we said,
"Beam me up, Scotty."

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.664
And you know, again,
Mandela effect.

00:03:52.664 --> 00:03:54.967
And we use the effect,
the beaming effect from

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:56.836
"Star Trek:
The Next Generation,"

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.004
which, of course,
Scotty wasn't in.

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.072
He was in the original.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.639
So for the person
who pointed that out,

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:01.808
I am sorry

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:03.376
[Nerdy voice]
that you're a nerd. [ Chuckles ]

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:05.444
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:07.179
[ Normal voice ]
We mentioned "Doctor Who,"

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:08.814
and the "Doctor Who" fans

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.850
reached out to say
we did a great job.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.585
No corrections needed.
Thank you.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:16.189
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:22.094
We mentioned
Werther's Originals,

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:23.929
the caramel hard candy.

00:04:23.929 --> 00:04:27.066
It's a German company.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.534
I was told by --

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.270
And I'm very happy that
we have international viewers.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:32.471
Let me start by that.

00:04:32.471 --> 00:04:35.074
But sometimes I think
they make a correction

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:38.711
based on their language,
not ours,

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:42.381
that the correct
way to pronounce Werther's --

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:43.549
the "H" is silent

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.551
and the "W" is pronounced
like a "V".

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:50.289
So, "Verter's,"
but I'm not gonna do that.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.658
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.658 --> 00:04:58.364
I would only do that
if I was saying,

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:01.467
[ Imitating German accent ]
"You will give me the name

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:06.105
of your network of agents.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:11.744
I recommend you do so
by the time I finished

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:12.945
this 'Verter's.'"

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:17.316
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:20.086
"You have more than an hour."
[ Laughs ]

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:23.923
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:31.164
Conserve, conserving.

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:34.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.137 --> 00:05:42.508
Speaking of Werther's --
"Verter's" --

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:45.077
we talked about how,

00:05:45.077 --> 00:05:49.448
if you shot Wether's --
"Verter's" -- out of a gun,

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:52.218
it would puncture Kevlar.

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:56.522
And someone wrote this.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:06:00.993
"Anything can penetrate Kevlar
if it's going fast enough.

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:04.830
The speed that a Werther's --
'Verter's' -- Original

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.365
would have to go
to penetrate Kevlar

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:14.206
is 37,908.55 meters per second
or 84,799.011 miles per hour,

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:18.844
which is almost 111 times
the speed of sound in air.

00:06:18.844 --> 00:06:21.780
This would make a Werther's --
'Verter's' -- Original

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:24.517
the third-fastest
manmade object ever,

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:27.386
placing it behind
a manhole cover --

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.421
look it up --
and before the Voyager 1

00:06:29.421 --> 00:06:33.059
deep-space probe,
with more than twice

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:35.428
Voyager 1's speed.

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:40.733
Sincerely,
a jackal with a calculator."

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:43.402
A jackal with a calculator,
or as we call them,

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:44.604
"a jaculater."

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:51.110
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.346
They get off on doing
their math problems.

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:56.916
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.518 --> 00:07:01.987
I have to correct
my own bad manners.

00:07:01.987 --> 00:07:04.356
Our dear friend, colleague,
Jimmy Kimmel

00:07:04.356 --> 00:07:07.326
tested positive for COVID.
Had to miss some shows.

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:10.696
Came back on Monday,
and in the monologue

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:14.000
spoke very kindly about
how many people reached out.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.968
Different late-night
hosts went so far as,

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.436
say Stephen Colbert,

00:07:17.436 --> 00:07:20.339
who does not surprise me,
a lovely man, sent him soup.

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:23.543
He then went on to say
that I did not reach out at all.

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:25.243
I have since reached out
to apologize, but I do --

00:07:25.243 --> 00:07:31.417
I'm also gonna fix
this soup problem, and, uh, I...

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:33.986
Devastated that I...

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:39.258
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.258 --> 00:07:41.159
...didn't think to do that.

00:07:41.159 --> 00:07:44.463
But we're gonna get it
out to our friend.

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:46.265
Some yummy soup.

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:48.134
Apologies, Jimmy.
Get well soon.

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:51.637
And get well soon to our friend
Stephen Colbert, as well.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:53.371
COVID does seem
to want to come

00:07:53.371 --> 00:07:55.007
for the late-night hosts.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.713
Milli Vanilli.

00:08:00.713 --> 00:08:03.748
Sore subject,
especially for Shoemaker.

00:08:03.748 --> 00:08:06.385
Used to travel around.

00:08:06.385 --> 00:08:08.187
You were like a Deadhead
for Milli Vanilli.

00:08:08.187 --> 00:08:12.992
[ Laughter ]

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:16.562
After.

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:18.564
You started following them
after the scandal.

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:21.867
[ Laughter ]

00:08:21.867 --> 00:08:23.436
"They got grit."

00:08:23.436 --> 00:08:24.836
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.836 --> 00:08:28.241
"Lot of people can't sing,
don't make it as singers."

00:08:28.241 --> 00:08:32.144
Um...

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:35.581
So anyway,
we had a Milli Vanilli reference

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:37.783
in the show, and then this
was just an accident,

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:41.386
but we played the track early,
before the callback, and I said,

00:08:41.386 --> 00:08:42.421
you know, that's what --

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:43.522
that's how they caught
Milli Vanilli --

00:08:43.522 --> 00:08:44.857
they played the track early.

00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:46.826
And we were playing
"Blame It on the Rain."

00:08:46.826 --> 00:08:49.795
So, couple of things.
Turns out people remember this.

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:52.264
The song was
"Girl, You Know It's True,"

00:08:52.264 --> 00:08:56.135
and it didn't start early.
It skipped.

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:57.703
That's how they caught
Milli Vanilli.

00:08:57.703 --> 00:08:59.204
And I think,
if you've ever watched it,

00:08:59.204 --> 00:09:04.176
it is -- it's crazy, because
they know in the moment

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:05.410
they're screwed.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:08.747
And it went a little bit
like this.

00:09:08.747 --> 00:09:10.683
[ Mouthing ]
♪ Girl, you know it's true ♪

00:09:10.683 --> 00:09:16.322
♪ True, true, true, true, true,
true, true, true, true ♪

00:09:16.322 --> 00:09:19.558
♪ True, true, true, true, true ♪

00:09:19.558 --> 00:09:21.527
♪ Ooh, ooh, ooh-ooh ♪

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:24.229
♪ I love you ♪

00:09:24.229 --> 00:09:25.564
[ Music stops ]

00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:30.936
[ Laughter ]

00:09:30.936 --> 00:09:33.339
A lot of people have been
saying, "Where's Wally?"

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:34.707
We're not talking about
Wally enough,

00:09:34.707 --> 00:09:37.843
I guess, on the show.
And, um...

00:09:37.843 --> 00:09:41.013
[ Laughter ]

00:09:41.013 --> 00:09:42.548
But we do try
to keep an eye out for Wally,

00:09:42.548 --> 00:09:46.118
to try to answer
that question, "Where's Wally?"

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:49.121
You might remember H.R.-gate...

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:51.023
[ Laughter ]

00:09:51.023 --> 00:09:54.226
...where Wally joined a Zoom
about H.R.,

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:56.795
Behavior in the Workplace,
and, uh...

00:09:56.795 --> 00:09:58.798
chose to do it in bed --
just a tiny little head

00:09:58.798 --> 00:10:00.566
in the corner of the frame.

00:10:00.566 --> 00:10:02.034
And we've given him a lot --
you know, we've given him

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:03.135
a lot of stick about that,

00:10:03.135 --> 00:10:05.771
and I think it was time
to move on.

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:08.140
But then Wally was discovered

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.142
waiting for his COVID
test results.

00:10:10.142 --> 00:10:11.710
I did not take these photos.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:14.413
[ Laughter ]

00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:15.681
But I had them sent to me.

00:10:15.681 --> 00:10:18.451
Wally once again
just making himself comfortable.

00:10:18.451 --> 00:10:24.156
[ Laughter ]

00:10:24.156 --> 00:10:25.791
Just look at --

00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:28.761
If we can zoom in,
just how happy Wally is.

00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:33.599
[ Laughter ]

00:10:33.599 --> 00:10:35.834
Uh...

00:10:35.834 --> 00:10:36.935
And I was like,
"What were you --

00:10:36.935 --> 00:10:38.237
What were you
on the phone doing?"

00:10:38.237 --> 00:10:41.474
You know what he told me?
"I was doing my makeup H.R."

00:10:41.474 --> 00:10:44.510
[ Laughter ]

00:10:47.646 --> 00:10:50.249
Also, we talked about a --

00:10:50.249 --> 00:10:56.455
that Trump would make
a hurricane wall in Texas

00:10:56.455 --> 00:10:59.825
out of -- out of Werther's --
"Verter's" --

00:10:59.825 --> 00:11:03.495
and people pointed out that if
you made a hurricane wall --

00:11:03.495 --> 00:11:05.964
This is what graphics
made for us.

00:11:05.964 --> 00:11:07.366
A hurricane wall --

00:11:07.366 --> 00:11:08.601
You would want to make
a hurricane wall

00:11:08.601 --> 00:11:09.835
against the ocean.

00:11:09.835 --> 00:11:11.770
That's where the hurricane
would come from.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:15.774
And instead, what they did is,
they made like a cage

00:11:15.774 --> 00:11:19.244
to catch the hurricane...
[ Laughter ]

00:11:19.244 --> 00:11:21.180
...and keep it from dissipating

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:22.915
and spreading out
into other states.

00:11:22.915 --> 00:11:25.984
So basically your friends
from graphics

00:11:25.984 --> 00:11:28.354
sentenced Texas to death.

00:11:28.354 --> 00:11:32.958
[ Laughter ]

00:11:32.958 --> 00:11:34.493
All right, I'm gonna --

00:11:34.493 --> 00:11:37.095
I'm not gonna call him anymore.

00:11:37.095 --> 00:11:40.866
I'm just gonna write Andy
and see if he's around.

00:11:40.866 --> 00:11:43.335
Uh...

00:11:43.335 --> 00:11:45.303
"I'm just gonna do this now.
You're on for 'Corrections,'"

00:11:45.303 --> 00:11:51.143
but I also want to read
what he texted me last week,

00:11:51.143 --> 00:11:53.945
obviously, during "Corrections."

00:11:53.945 --> 00:11:57.383
He wrote, "I'm naked.
Just got out of shower.

00:11:57.383 --> 00:11:59.951
Tell them I got Queen Bee."

00:11:59.951 --> 00:12:02.154
And then we finished
"Corrections,"

00:12:02.154 --> 00:12:04.657
and I was leaving,
and he wrote again,

00:12:04.657 --> 00:12:08.894
"Did you tell them?"
Very important.

00:12:08.894 --> 00:12:12.598
And then I wrote, "I did."
And he wrote,

00:12:12.598 --> 00:12:16.936
"But did you couch it in a burn?
I'm fine with it either way."

00:12:16.936 --> 00:12:18.370
And then I wrote,
"There was an eyeroll,

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.406
but I did say it like you
wrote it," which I did.

00:12:20.406 --> 00:12:22.341
I read it exactly that.

00:12:22.341 --> 00:12:24.977
And he wrote,
"And that I was naked?"

00:12:24.977 --> 00:12:26.712
Question mark, question mark,
question mark.

00:12:26.712 --> 00:12:28.313
And I wrote, "Yeah."

00:12:28.313 --> 00:12:31.684
And then Andy wrote,
"Did everyone get boners?"

00:12:31.684 --> 00:12:34.954
[ Laughter ]

00:12:34.954 --> 00:12:37.689
"Did everyone get boners???"

00:12:37.689 --> 00:12:40.959
And I wrote,
"I'll follow up next week."

00:12:40.959 --> 00:12:44.830
And he wrote, "Joke's on them.
If they did, I look like crap."

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:49.368
[ Laughter ]

00:12:51.169 --> 00:12:54.707
All right.

00:12:54.707 --> 00:12:57.209
Last thing.
Might not hear back from him.

00:12:57.209 --> 00:12:58.543
Probably should have
texted him earlier.

00:12:58.543 --> 00:13:02.915
You know, like I said,
I'm out of sorts today.

00:13:02.915 --> 00:13:06.184
This is very lovely, though.

00:13:06.184 --> 00:13:09.221
And I think it speaks
to a kind of best and worst

00:13:09.221 --> 00:13:13.525
of what we're dealing with
with our -- with this whole --

00:13:13.525 --> 00:13:15.027
I don't know --
this whole thing.

00:13:15.027 --> 00:13:16.861
Someone wrote, "If there's
anyone from the Late Night team

00:13:16.861 --> 00:13:19.031
reading this --"
there was -- me --

00:13:19.031 --> 00:13:21.333
"Seth was supposed to perform
in Manchester, New Hampshire,

00:13:21.333 --> 00:13:23.402
right as COVID started --"
true --

00:13:23.402 --> 00:13:24.737
"and the show was postponed."

00:13:24.737 --> 00:13:26.705
Also true.
"When it was rescheduled,

00:13:26.705 --> 00:13:29.141
like a year and a half later,
my best friend that was supposed

00:13:29.141 --> 00:13:32.878
to go with me the first time
couldn't make it.

00:13:32.878 --> 00:13:35.814
And I asked a friend/co-worker
who has a really great sense

00:13:35.814 --> 00:13:37.516
of humor to come with me
last-minute.

00:13:37.516 --> 00:13:42.554
He and I
are now getting married in July.

00:13:42.554 --> 00:13:44.690
And it is a direct result
of hanging out at the show.

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:47.259
Thank you, Seth,
for giving me my husband."

00:13:47.259 --> 00:13:48.894
So lovely.

00:13:48.894 --> 00:13:51.297
And I just want to say
congratulations to you both.

00:13:51.297 --> 00:13:53.332
This wasn't the right place
to write that.

00:13:53.332 --> 00:14:00.139
[ Laughter ]

00:14:00.139 --> 00:14:03.175
Now we have, of course,
good people

00:14:03.175 --> 00:14:05.643
amongst the jackals
who live in the comments.

00:14:05.643 --> 00:14:07.045
One of them wrote,
"This is lovely.

00:14:07.045 --> 00:14:09.381
Hope you find all the happiness
in the world together."

00:14:09.381 --> 00:14:13.519
Appropriate.
Kind of thing you should say.

00:14:13.519 --> 00:14:14.687
Another jackal thought,

00:14:14.687 --> 00:14:16.856
"Oh, they want to know
what I think."

00:14:16.856 --> 00:14:17.989
They wrote,
"You're getting married

00:14:17.989 --> 00:14:20.359
after less than a year
of dating?"

00:14:20.359 --> 00:14:22.394
[ Laughter ]

00:14:22.394 --> 00:14:25.897
Bro, take it up with me.

00:14:25.897 --> 00:14:27.732
But leave those people alone.

00:14:27.732 --> 00:14:29.234
But then there's my
favorite kind of people,

00:14:29.234 --> 00:14:31.369
which is the jackals
for the jackals,

00:14:31.369 --> 00:14:32.871
who wrote, "They're co-workers.

00:14:32.871 --> 00:14:35.974
They've probably known
each other a few years."

00:14:35.974 --> 00:14:38.744
[ Laughter ]

00:14:38.744 --> 00:14:40.746
Mostly, I'm just
very happy for them.

00:14:40.746 --> 00:14:45.184
I'm sorry we don't have Samberg.

00:14:45.184 --> 00:14:46.852
Hold on.
I'm gonna try my other one.

00:14:46.852 --> 00:14:55.260
[ FaceTime ringing ]

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:58.564
This person lives in L.A.,

00:14:58.564 --> 00:15:01.667
and last week, after -- after --
'cause I don't plan ahead,

00:15:01.667 --> 00:15:04.970
I wrote, "Hey, I called you
for 'Corrections,'"

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.940
and they said,
"Oh, remember, I'm in L.A.

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:09.608
I was probably asleep."

00:15:09.608 --> 00:15:12.177
And I was like,
"Well, we do it at 5:00."

00:15:12.177 --> 00:15:14.212
[ Laughter ]

00:15:14.212 --> 00:15:16.548
And they said, "Yeah."

00:15:16.548 --> 00:15:20.752
[ Laughter ]

00:15:20.752 --> 00:15:23.288 line:0%
We had a lot of fun today.

00:15:23.288 --> 00:15:27.226 line:0%
We're going to come back
hard next week and...

00:15:29.862 --> 00:15:31.463
I'm pretty happy about this one.

00:15:31.463 --> 00:15:32.931
[ Laughs ]

00:15:32.931 --> 00:15:36.167
[ Laughter ]

00:15:36.167 --> 00:15:37.236
We'll see you next week.

